patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Supersedes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113640\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13793\r\n\r\nThis is an alternative version of #113640 where we use a shader instead of a mesh to show the inaccessible areas.\r\n\r\nThe benefits is the shader version has smooth corners while the previous version was only done triangle by triangle sections of a sphere.\r\n\r\n[ik_humanoid.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25401769/ik_humanoid.zip)\r\n\r\n> Disclaimer: this problem was developed by multiple developers from 2016 to 2020 to 2026 with  the developer @EGjoni Eron Gjoni's original research on inverse kinematic systems in Java Processing.\r\n>\r\n> * https://github.com/EGjoni/Everything-Will-Be-IK\r\n> * https://github.com/V-Sekai/many_bone_ik/tree/main/design_docs\r\n> \r\n> Special thanks to @TokageItLab for assisting with multi-cone visualization usability research, however we reverted to the original shader from EGjoni/Everything-Will-Be-IK migrated to a Godot Engine gdshader.\r\n> \r\n> I identified and verified the solution, but some root cause analysis and implementation was performed on Cursor IDE.\r\n> \r\n> Used to determine the boundaries for the kusudama boundary shader \"dark green\" vs \"light green\"\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116456/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116456/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}